boethius-foreknowledge.md:1: argue/converse: boethius-foreknowledge.logic.r3.3 P2 (S3): the sentence makes the words after "no" the condition, but P2 has them follow from it: it reads "if necessarily, that which providence foresees to be about to happen comes to pass, then it is not so that there is freedom of the will"
